  "description": "Installation of a text-based art work (title TBC) by the artist Zineb Sedira on the external wall of a studio building in the 3 Mills Studios complex, in the south west of the site. \n\n'Dreams are a language made of images. In cinema, every object and light means something, as in a dream'. \n\nThe installation is based on a quote by Federico Fellini, the famous Italian filmmaker. It speaks to the context of 3 Mills Studios and the important role it has played in the world of film, TV and theatre production for many years. The artist, Zineb Sedira, works across the mediums of photography, film, installation and performance, and is well known for her explorations of the human effects of geography, as well as referencing film from the 50's and 60's. \n\nThe text installation will reference old American outdoor cinema signage and will be made from DiBond letters, attached to steel box section 'rails' which in turn will fix to the walls by means of a bracket and telescopic arm system to allow the letters to sit slightly proud of the staggered wall, allowing for the sun to cast shadows as it moves round the building. \n\nThe intention is for The Line to launch the art installation during London Sculpture week in September 2025 - this is a an initiative which celebrates the capital’s vibrant creative spirit by transforming public spaces with striking outdoor sculptures. Running from 20 to 28 September, the event unites four major cultural initiatives – Frieze Sculpture, the Fourth Plinth, Sculpture in the City, and The Line – to invigorate the city’s public spaces and highlight the transformative power of public art in the city.",
